A||N||4||NPlack||Turbocharging on a Stock EFI||||5||
Z||000000||NPlack||05-23-2001||05:59 PM||||Okay, here is a thought for using twin turbo's on a 2.8 or 3.1 motor...<P>Fist off, the engine would have to be beefed up to accomidate the turbo's, but that is not what this post is about.<P>What i would like to know is:<BR>If i replace the stock fuel injectors on a Multi-port 2.8 or 3.1 to double flow size injectors, install a 1Bar map sensor, and install a boost-regulated fuel pressure regulator, will the Stock EFI be able to account for this?  I am planning on using twin Thunderbird turbo's set at 15PSI, and running an intercooler.<P>If this would not work, can the stock computer be retuned?  Or will i have to buy an aftermarket one?<P>You may ask why don't i just use an aftermarket computer.  Here's why:   $$$$$!  I am trying to do a budget Hi-PO performance car, and don;t have $3K to blow on a Speed=Pro EFI computer.<P>Thanks in advance!<P>-Plack||||reg||5
Z||000001||BV MotorSports||05-23-2001||10:23 PM||||Why in the world would you even attempt a twin turbo set-up and try to keep it cheap?<BR>Not cheap or easy.<P>@ 15 psi of boost your pistons would crumble, head gaskets would call it quits and thermo-nuclear melt down would occur.<P>Ok well maybe not that bad but OUCH, it would leave a mark!<P>A basic turbo set-up like Dennis L. has is simple and cost effective. Do you know anyone that has a turbo'd fiero? Take a ride, you will be very surprised. If you follow Dennis' plans there is NOTHING you could do to your fiero that would be worth more hp for the dollar this side of N20.<P>Twin turbo is a cool idea but way too much plumbing and heat soak issues to deal with.<BR>As soon as the 2.8 dies in my 87GT I will be upgrading to a 3.8 n/a. (best engine swap for the $$$ PERIOD). Once I get it done I will start on a turbo kit for it. Think of an intercooled Mitsu 20g equipped 3.8 fiero! Bring on those v8 Fieros!<P> I have done some v8 swaps and while not knocking them...do you really need the hassle? Its a compromise any way you look at it no matter what any of the v8 kit guys claim. The only reason to step up to a v8 is for bragging/wow factor. Nothing more. The only v8 I would consider swapping would be a LT1 or LS1. But neither are cheap to buy and to install.<P>Check out Dennis' page and good luck.<P>Steven<P>------------------<BR>87 Fiero GT 14.9/ 93mph<BR>94 Formula WS6 w/ NOS 12.4 /118mph<BR>87 Conquest TSi <BR>85.5 Starion ESi||||reg||1
Z||000002||cadaver||05-23-2001||10:55 PM||||I think dennis had the prom chip burned to run with a turbo. I also remember that the early ecm's were built to be able to turbo. I think the thought they might do it.<BR>You will also need a timing retard. Like a MSD BTM or better yet a 6BTM which is a 6AL with the boost timing master built in. You have to retard the timing under boost conditions. <BR>If you use a T3 from a thunderbird be sure to get the water cooled one. I dont think they all are.||||reg||1
Z||000003||NPlack||05-23-2001||11:01 PM||||Haha, figured someone would question the integrity of this motor.  I have that covered.  I plan on investing in a set of forged pistons, and a hi-po gasket and a set of ARP studs.  Might possible have a friend O-ring it.<P>Anyways, hate to say it, but it is not going on a Fiero.  Ack!  Might have lost all respect there.  I plan on putting it in some sort of cavalier or sunbird.  More hood space.  Also, more room.  Sorry guys.  Posted this because i knew you all run 2.8's and 3.1's.  Knew you had an excellent knowlege base.  In any case, i hope i can get some pointers on the computers.<P>-Plack||||reg||3
Z||000004||NPlack||05-23-2001||11:04 PM||||What is Dennis' site?  I would like to look at it.<P>-Plack||||reg||1
